  "raw_response": null,
  "cot_trace": " I'm working through the relationship between independent sets and triangles in graph complements. An independent set of size 3 means three vertices with no edges between them, which translates to a triangle in the complement graph. By Ramsey theory, any graph on 6 or more vertices must contain either a triangle or an independent set of size 3, so on 8 vertices the complement needs to be triangle-free.\n\nFor the constraint \u03b1(G) \u2264 2, the complement must be triangle-free, which is achievable with 8 vertices. The simplest solution is just taking the complete graph K_8, which has independence number 1 and connectivity 7.",
